# A trait value meets a bound of its own trait on every tier: a
# `Pair<Describe>` takes `impl Pair<T: Describe>.Describe`, and a
# `[Describe]` is passed to `fn<T: Describe>(xs: [T])`. Sema compares the
# trait identities, not their spellings: the value's trait is held under its
# module-qualified name and the bound is written bare.
# trait_value_as_another_trait_is_refused.case keeps the other side: a
# trait value never meets another trait's bound.
fixture: TraitValueMeetsItsOwnBound.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step: jet run -O0 pair.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "pair #1\n"
step: jet run -O1 pair.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "pair #1\n"
step: jet run -O2 pair.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "pair #1\n"
step: jet run -O0 list.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "[#1, #2]\n"
step: jet run -O1 list.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "[#1, #2]\n"
step: jet run -O2 list.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "[#1, #2]\n"
